{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792445785,"nonce":"3c8Voe/e+D6RCH0WIuwPmVfbzuE=","message":"Producer verification at sibling ABI a92f5c0: generate_masks.py runs the unchanged encoder against local Blinc crates, without access shims or sibling edits. Ten scenes at scales 1 and 2 emit actual layer tables with 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 25, 27, 33, 37 and 4099 stops. The generator asserts the table count in emitted data. The 4099-stop table spans texture rows.\n\nImplemented mask ownership, record parsing and retained GPU upload in display_list/mask.rs. effects.rs reexports LayerMask and MAX_MASK_STOPS for the existing module paths. LayerMask::stops is an Arc slice, so cloning/moving layers shares stop storage; LayerMask and LayerFx are Clone rather than Copy. MAX_MASK_STOPS remains 16 as the inline-uniform capacity, not a supported-mask limit. Checked table arithmetic rejects nonfinite/fractional indices and counts, zero counts, truncated ranges, invalid kind/spread and nonfinite stop values before allocation. The malformed-table and flattening tests now use invalid data to request fallback rather than relying on a valid 17-stop table being unsupported.\n\nAt most 16 stops keep their existing uniform path. Larger masks pack two offset/alpha pairs into each RGBA32Float texel; the composite uses unfiltered textureLoad across rows. LayerEffects retains one growable table and upload buffer, updates it before each submitted composite and shares its existing layout/pass machinery. The placeholder is one texel, 16 bytes. The 17-stop case grows the GPU table to 256 bytes; the 4099-stop case reaches 1024 by 4 texels, 64 KiB, retained for reuse. The layer uniform remains 768 bytes. There is no new render pass, render target or primitive/image field; their layouts stay 544/208 bytes. GPU texture dimension and allocation limits still apply, as for other renderer resources. No performance benchmark was requested or run.\n\nThe independent raw-record oracle samples alpha from producer tables, applies the inverse mask frame and spread, then composites quantized premultiplied layers with their filter matrices and opacity. Twenty-four render cases compare every RGBA channel at scales 1 and 2, with one Painter crossing 16/17, growing to multirow storage, shrinking tables, returning to uniforms and nesting different masks under affine transforms. Worst error is 1/255 in every case, without skipped probes. They use consumer-owned images so they also exercise the no-storage-buffer path independently of the SDF packing debt.\n\nThe nested case exposed an existing origin error: moving a child layer into its cropped parent target moved the content/bounds but not the child mask mapping. It differed by 67/255. Moving mask translation by target displacement divided by display scale fixes it; stop tables remain shared. Normal and forced vertex-buffer GPU suites both pass all 32 display-list tests. With both storage flags off and capacities 1024, all 24 new mask render cases pass on Apple M1 Pro, Metal. This does not fix or validate the primitive DT packing in ce34b20, actual WebGL2, or PowerVR/Adreno/mobile pixels.\n\nMutation checks fail by 92/255 when the stop count is capped at 16, 92/255 when texture row reads are forced to zero, and 121/255 when uploads are skipped after table capacity is reused. The prior untranslated nested mapping failed by 67/255. All temporary mutations and capability overrides are restored. GPU-free integration: 101 passed. Full workspace gate is running; final results will follow.","files":null}]}